  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Belleric acid and the CD276 antigen, mediated through the HaCaT cell line. Belleric acid is identified as a target of multiple compounds, including 5,7,3',4',5'-Pentahydroxy-3,6,8-trimethoxyflavone and (1R,4R)-4-Hydroxydauca-7-Ene-6,9-Dione, all of which are known to target the CD276 antigen. This indicates that Belleric acid may act as a modulator or activator of the CD276 pathway, possibly through the activation of downstream signaling cascades in HaCaT cells. The varying scores across the three paths suggest that the strength of the relationship may depend on the specific compound involved, with Belleric acid showing a moderate level of interaction with the CD276 pathway. The evidence is consistent with a role for Belleric acid in influencing CD276 expression or function, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction.",
